       "blockId": "3468405b18",
       "blockName": "Story Para",
       "children": [],
       "classes": [],
       "customAttributes": {},
       "element": "p",
       "innerHTML": "The bus dropped us where the tar gave up, at a chai stall whose owner has watched forty years of walkers set out too fast. He poured, looked at our shoes, and said we'd learn.",
       "mobileStyles": {
        "fontSize": "17px"
       },
       "rawStyles": {},
       "tabletStyles": {}
      },
      {
       "attributes": {},
       "baseStyles": {
        "color": "var(--55ee66ff-0002-4e02-8e02-eeff0002dd02, #171412)",
        "fontFamily": "Newsreader",
        "fontSize": "19px",
        "fontWeight": "400",
        "height": "fit-content",
        "lineHeight": "1.85",
        "maxWidth": "680px",
        "width": "fit-content"
       },
       "blockId": "003795f6fe",
       "blockName": "Story Para",
       "children": [],
       "classes": [],
       "customAttributes": {},
       "element": "p",
       "innerHTML": "The path climbs through betel groves the maps have stopped naming. Every hour or so it forgets it's a path and becomes a stream bed, a threshing floor, somebody's yard with a dog who has seen it all before.",
       "mobileStyles": {
        "fontSize": "17px"
       },
       "rawStyles": {},
       "tabletStyles": {}
      },
      {
       "attributes": {},
       "baseStyles": {
        "borderLeftColor": "var(--55ee66ff-0005-4e05-8e05-eeff0005dd05, #0E7A5F)",
        "borderLeftStyle": "solid",
        "borderLeftWidth": "3px",
        "color": "var(--55ee66ff-0002-4e02-8e02-eeff0002dd02, #171412)",
        "fontFamily": "Newsreader",
        "fontSize": "40px",
        "fontStyle": "italic",
        "fontWeight": "500",
        "height": "fit-content",
        "letterSpacing": "-0.02em",
        "lineHeight": "1.3",
        "maxWidth": "760px",
        "padding": "8px 0px 8px 32px",
        "width": "fit-content"
